{"id":"n-20261015-nkggj6","category":"world","display_title":"US Considers Massive Bomb Against Iran","display_title_he":"ארה\"ב שוקלת שימוש בפצצה ענקית נגד איראן","short_summary":"The Pentagon has drawn up options to use the massive GBU-43 bomb against Iranian nuclear and energy sites. Doubts remain over whether the weapon can penetrate deeply buried underground bunkers.","english_level":"C1","words":480,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/news/article/hksqbr6igg","title":"דיווח: ארה\"ב שוקלת להשתמש לראשונה ב\"אם כל הפצצות\" מול איראן","published_at":"2026-10-15T04:15:35.000Z"},{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001559614","title":"דיווח: ארה\"ב שוקלת להשתמש ב\"אם כל הפצצות\" נגד איראן","published_at":"2026-10-15T04:43:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-15T04:15:35.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-15T05:50:11.408Z","quality_score":8,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The United States military has drafted updated contingency strike plans against Iran that include the potential deployment of the GBU-43/B Massive Ordnance Air Blast, widely recognized as the \"Mother of All Bombs,\" according to American officials cited by CNN. These operational packages were reportedly devised in the event that President Donald Trump issues orders to resume offensive military operations against the Islamic Republic, whether prior to or following the midterm elections. Deploying this weapon, the most destructive conventional munition in the American arsenal, would represent a dramatic escalation in the confrontation between Washington and Tehran.","According to informed defense sources, Trump instructed the armed forces to assemble supplementary strike packages directed at numerous Iranian energy infrastructure assets and fortified nuclear facilities. One official noted that internal operational guidance described the potential offensive as occurring before an eventual American military withdrawal from the area of responsibility governed by United States Central Command, or CENTCOM. Such language suggests that the administration might contemplate launching a fresh wave of bombardments, declaring a strategic triumph, and promptly pulling forces out of the region.","Operational blueprints explicitly envision targeting Iranian nuclear complexes, most notably the Pickaxe Mountain site, which Trump has repeatedly threatened in recent months. Both American and Israeli intelligence authorities believe that Tehran has stowed critical components of its nuclear program deep inside the mountain. However, defense officials privy to internal Pentagon assessments harbor considerable doubts regarding whether the weapon could effectively accomplish Trump’s stated strategic goals or shift the overarching balance of the conflict. Military observers and defense analysts have questioned whether the massive bomb could penetrate deeply enough underground to demolish facilities shielded beneath thick granite formations, suggesting the munition might ultimately serve as little more than a psychological instrument.","The GBU-43/B traces its origin back to the early 2000s, with development commencing in 2002 ahead of the war in Iraq and undergoing its maiden test in 2003. Broader production of guided bomb units gained momentum during the 1990s, driven by the proliferation of GPS technology that enabled maximum delivery precision, though these systems were principally designed to devastate surface installations rather than fortified underground bunkers. Packed with approximately eleven tons of high explosives, the GPS-guided munition creates an expansive blast radius capable of flattening an area equivalent to nine urban city blocks.","Given its extraordinary bulk and weight, the weapon cannot be carried by standard fighter-bombers; instead, a C-130 Hercules transport aircraft serves as its sole delivery platform. In combat, the munition is rolled out from the aircraft's rear cargo ramp before utilizing satellite signals to steer toward its intended destination. To date, the weapon has seen operational deployment on just one occasion, when American forces dropped it against subterranean Islamic State tunnel networks in Afghanistan in 2017. As Washington evaluates its options, debate persists over whether deploying such a colossal weapon against hardened Iranian facilities would yield tangible military results."],"facts":[{"fact":"The United States military has formulated strike plans against Iranian energy infrastructure and nuclear facilities that include the potential use of the GBU-43/B MOAB.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The plans were devised in case President Donald Trump orders strikes before or after the midterm elections.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The GBU-43/B is the largest non-nuclear munition in the United States military inventory.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Internal planning phrased the strikes as taking place before an American withdrawal from the CENTCOM area of responsibility.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Strike plans specifically include the Pickaxe Mountain nuclear site, which the US and Israel believe houses nuclear program components.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Military officials and analysts have questioned the MOAB's effectiveness against underground facilities protected by granite, noting it was designed for surface destruction.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The weapon carries about eleven tons of explosives, is guided by GPS, and must be deployed from a C-130 Hercules cargo aircraft.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The MOAB has been used operationally only once, against Islamic State tunnels in Afghanistan in 2017.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"United States","lemma":"United States","pos":"name","he":"ארצות הברית","name":true},{"text":"military","lemma":"military","pos":"noun","he":"צבא","name":false},{"text":"drafted","lemma":"draft","pos":"verb","he":"גיבש, ניסח","name":false},{"text":"updated","lemma":"updated","pos":"adjective","he":"מעודכן","name":false},{"text":"contingency","lemma":"contingency","pos":"noun","he":"חירום, מקרה אפשרי","name":false},{"text":"strike plans","lemma":"strike plan","pos":"compound","he":"תוכניות תקיפה","name":false},{"text":"Iran","lemma":"Iran","pos":"name","he":"איראן","name":true},{"text":"potential","lemma":"potential","pos":"adjective","he":"פוטנציאלי, אפשרי","name":false},{"text":"deployment","lemma":"deployment","pos":"noun","he":"פריסה, שימוש מבצעי","name":false},{"text":"GBU-43/B","lemma":"GBU-43/B","pos":"name","he":"GBU-43/B (דגם פצצה)","name":true},{"text":"Massive Ordnance Air Blast","lemma":"Massive Ordnance Air Blast","pos":"name","he":"פצצת MOAB","name":true},{"text":"widely","lemma":"widely","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן נרחב","name":false},{"text":"recognized","lemma":"recognize","pos":"verb","he":"מוכר","name":false},{"text":"Mother of All Bombs","lemma":"Mother of All Bombs","pos":"name","he":"\"אם כל הפצצות\"","name":true},{"text":"according to","lemma":"according to","pos":"other","he":"לפי, על פי","name":false},{"text":"American","lemma":"American","pos":"adjective","he":"אמריקאי","name":false},{"text":"officials","lemma":"official","pos":"noun","he":"בכירים, גורמים רשמיים","name":false},{"text":"cited","lemma":"cite","pos":"verb","he":"צוטט","name":false},{"text":"CNN","lemma":"CNN","pos":"name","he":"סי-אן-אן","name":true},{"text":"operational","lemma":"operational","pos":"adjective","he":"מבצעי","name":false},{"text":"packages","lemma":"package","pos":"noun","he":"חבילות (פעולה/תקיפה)","name":false},{"text":"reportedly","lemma":"reportedly","pos":"adverb","he":"על פי הדיווחים","name":false},{"text":"devised","lemma":"devise","pos":"verb","he":"פותח, גובש","name":false},{"text":"in the event that","lemma":"in the event that","pos":"idiom","he":"במקרה ש-","name":false},{"text":"President","lemma":"president","pos":"noun","he"